      "key": {
        "uuid": "0b5991ab_4360d073",
        "filename": "zephyr/shim/src/watchdog.c",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 172,
      "author": {
        "id": 1478788
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-01-21T10:37:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "there\u0027s a `k_uptime_get_32` too if you want the truncated version",
      "parentUuid": "af71bac5_8d8be214",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 172,
        "startChar": 22,
        "endLine": 172,
        "endChar": 25
      },
      "revId": "3526d04d18036c1aef9f81347731eff7c823cded",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7332e3aa_4bdb4868",
        "filename": "zephyr/shim/src/watchdog.c",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 172,
      "author": {
        "id": 1390635
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-01-21T23:12:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`now` is 64-bits because `watchdog_reload_period_max_ts_ms` is 64-bits. `watchdog_reload_period_max_ts_ms` is 64-bits because it holds an absolute timestamp. Elapsed only needs to be 32 bit because it\u0027s just the elapsed time since the last reload. \n\n`watchdog_reload_last_ts_ms` has been updated to also be 64 bit.",
      "parentUuid": "0b5991ab_4360d073",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 172,
        "startChar": 22,
        "endLine": 172,
        "endChar": 25
      },
      "revId": "3526d04d18036c1aef9f81347731eff7c823cded",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "79cc307a_39615ac7",
        "filename": "zephyr/shim/src/watchdog.c",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 349,
      "author": {
        "id": 1479762
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-01-21T06:03:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Printing from inside the spinlock could take time, which might lead to `watchdog_reload()` to stall before \"feeding\" the WD. I propose to copy the values to local variables and then print outside of spinlock.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 349,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 349,
        "endChar": 8
      },
      "revId": "3526d04d18036c1aef9f81347731eff7c823cded",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
